From 7ebc3abb3e8ca5ccfb73073a98e0ee8d5e1b7731 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:40:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] world: read gameplay-facts.json state by state for the block
 tables

Behaviours::load (the world generator's copy, on a launch with no table
snapshot yet: the first of every new build) parsed the 55 MB
gameplay-facts.json whole into a serde_json::Value: 540 MiB, held while
the tables were built, on top of the rest of the load. On a 1 GB handheld
the game was killed there.

Keep each state only as the GameplayProjection the client's own path
already uses: one state's tree at a time, the rows a few MiB. The
projection moves down to horizon-world and takes any
GameplayStateSource, so its fields are read through the same getters.

R36S with 746 MB available, first launch: killed in 4 of 4 runs before,
now through at a peak of 560 MB, 256 MB still available.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
